  "answer": "An account executive should correct the informal \"immediate deletion\" claim and give the official standard timeline from the Security and Data Governance Policy. The AE should explain that although access is revoked immediately upon termination, physical deletion follows a longer schedule: primary database and active storage deletion completes within 90 days of contract termination, and full cryptographic erasure of cold storage backups completes within 120 days of contract termination due to the 30-day backup rotation cycle [NL-007-S06]. The AE should also qualify that standard deletion is executed within 90 days [NL-007-S06], and faster, custom deletion windows (e.g., 30-day active purge and 60-day backup purge) are available only to enterprise clients if explicitly documented in a signed Data Processing Agreement (DPA) and configured by the engineering operations team [NL-007-S06] [NL-019-S05] [NL-019-S07]. The AE must not overpromise immediate deletion and should cite the official policy instead [NL-032-S06].\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer\nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
